	"about": {
		"text": "The whey left after milk is curdled with acid instead of rennet, from fresh cheeses such as cottage cheese and quark, from Greek-style yogurt, or from acid casein. It has a pH of about 4.3–5, against roughly 6 for sweet whey, and is rich in calcium phosphate and lactic acid, which make it hard to dry.",
